@startuml Import chain

!pragma teoz true

title Import chain (gontroller): walk -> group -> gate -> identify -> exif -> commit;\nevery participant is a step (own goroutine), every arrow is a typed pipe (values + the walk's flush)

box "walk: the files" #LightCyan
control "walk\n(the entry)" as Walker
end box

box "group: whole assets (a sub-chain)" #LightCyan
control "switch\n(first that claims)" as Groups
control "Apple Photos\ngrouper" as Photos
control "plain folder\ngrouper (last)" as Generic
end box

box "gate: the files table" #LightGreen
control "gate" as Gate
end box

box "identify: the item known (exiftool lives here)" #Lavender
control "read\n(exiftool, N)" as Exif
control "classify" as Mime
control "merge" as Merge
control "fingerprint" as Fingerprint
control "validate" as Validator #LightGreen
control "embedded\n(exiftool)" as Embedded
control "sizes" as Sizes
control "pick\n(cheap preview)" as Preview #LightYellow
control "yield" as Yield
end box

box "exif: the EXIF perceptors, their values kept" #Honeydew
control "built in\n(exif_date, exif_size, ...)" as Core
control "external\n(.so)" as Plugins
control "keep\n(the perceptors' values)" as Keep
end box

box "commit: the item published" #MistyRose
control "close" as Closer
end box

box "importer (the top)" #WhiteSmoke
control "the passes,\nRefresh" as Top
end box

database "DB" as DB

== files flow in; groups flow out one by one, steps run concurrently ==

Top -> Walker: Chain.Run: a pass starts the entry

loop every file under the root
    Walker -> DB: its row: created / stat refreshed,\nCheckTime (Changed: new or stat changed)
    Walker -> Groups: *dto.FileDto (the row)
    note left of Walker
    Unreadable directory:
    skipped, recorded (V1)
    end note
end

alt Apple claims it (inside *.photoslibrary)
    Groups -> Photos: file
    Photos -> Photos: first file: asset links from Photos.sqlite\n(original, render, Live Photo video); buffer of open\ngroups, a group goes out when all its files arrived
    Photos -> Gate: providers.Asset (asset UUID; a file of an asset\ntrashed / hidden in Photos: sent as gone)
else nobody else claims it (other providers: Immich, ... later)
    Groups -> Generic: file
    Generic -> Generic: sidecars by name, next to each other\n(buffer: one open group; a complete group goes out)
    Generic -> Gate: providers.Asset
end
note over Groups: a provider not enabled is not asked:\nits files are a plain folder's

alt a gone file
    Gate -> DB: the model's Gone: a main file's item deleted,\na sidecar's item Dirty
else unchanged, the model says no work (NeedsWork)
    Gate ->x Gate: drop
else changed (stat, a role the grouper gave) / needs work (Rework, ...)
    Gate -> Exif: gate.Group (no provider type past here)
end

Exif -> Exif: ONE exiftool -j call for the group,\nonly the declared tags (the perceptors'\nExifTags + identify's own); a map per file
Exif -> Mime: draft (private to identify)
Mime -> Mime: kind of every file\n(exif MIMEType, own extension table,\ncontent sniff), rank: main file, roles
Mime -> Merge: ranked draft
Merge -> Merge: the metadata package: a tag from\nthe source (Photos DB) > .xmp > main > derivatives;\nonly the perceptors' tags
Merge -> Fingerprint: + package
Fingerprint -> Fingerprint: the main file's bytes:\nsize + sha256(first, last 64 KB)
Fingerprint -> Validator: + fingerprint

Validator -> DB: by path and fingerprint:\nsame / changed / moved / duplicate
Validator -> Embedded: item (GUID) + draft

Embedded -> Embedded: nothing in the group shows:\nthe main file's embedded preview\n(exiftool -b into the cache)
Embedded -> Sizes: + embedded ("" = none)
Sizes -> DB: pixels, codec of every file
Sizes -> Preview: + sizes
Preview -> Preview: what the browser shows now, no transcode:\nShow / the main file (JPEG, PNG, ...; H.264 video) /\nthe biggest viewable derivative / the embedded one;\nany size counts
Preview -> Yield: + preview ("" = nothing yet)
Yield -> Core: identify.Item (the item + its metadata package;\nthe draft stays in identify)
Core -> Plugins: + date, size, length (written into the item)
Plugins -> Keep: + the external perceptors' values (read-only)
Keep -> DB: a row in every import perceptor's storage
Keep -> Closer: item
Closer -> DB: Visible (a preview) or Waiting (none)
note right of Closer
The client gets Visible (and Ready)
items at once. Ready comes later from
the expensive chain (transcode, fed
from the DB; roadmap: thumbnails)
end note

== end of walk ==

loop every row the walk did not stamp that it says is gone (V2: a complete walk,\nunder the root, not under unreadable directories)
    Walker -> Groups: *dto.FileDto (Gone): to its provider's grouper,\nwhich passes it through (or makes something of it)
end
Walker -> Groups: FLUSH
Groups -> Photos: flush
& Groups -> Generic: flush
note right of Groups: to every grouper (Route)
Generic -> Gate: what it holds (last group), flush
Photos -> Gate: flush (an incomplete group waits for the next walk)
note over Gate: once every grouper has flushed (the chain's barrier)\nthe flush goes on, through every step, to the end
note over Core, Keep: keep: on the flush, the perceptors' rows\nof gone items pruned (the previous walk's)
Closer --> Top: Chain.Run returns: the flush reached the chain's end (commit):\nevery group of the walk went through every step
Top -> Top: rescan pause (1 min), then the next pass

== One asset again (Apple Photos on demand) ==
note over Photos: Photos made a file of an asset local\n(the viewer asked for it: PhotoKit)
Photos -> Top: Refresh(uuid)
Top -> DB: MarkRework (updated_at untouched: no delta brings\nthe item back); the next pass processes it (NeedsWork)
note over Top: no waiting: the client guesses meanwhile\n(the tile's cloud goes once it got the original)

@enduml
